<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Marsaglia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1693</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war">Nine Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Marsaglia was fought on 4 October 1693 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war">Nine Years' War</a>. A French army under Marshal Catinat defeated the allied army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-ii">Victor Amadeus II</a> of Savoy with Spanish and imperial troops. The defeat left Piedmont open to plunder and contributed to Savoy's separate peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1696.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-marsaglia.jpg" alt="Battle of Marsaglia" width="320" height="271" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eugène Devéria · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_de_La_Marsaille,_4_octobre_1693.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
